    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just burnout tho. it feels deeper than that. like the actual substance of who i was is gone. i look at my old work and it feels like i'm looking at a stranger's life. if the thing that made me, *me*, is gone... what am i actually supposed to do with the rest of my time? it feels like i'm just waiting for nothing.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This sense of loss of self can feel profoundly confusing and scary, like grieving a part of your identity. It might be helpful to shift the focus away from what you *used to be* and focus instead on what you are experiencing *right now*. Consider exploring very small, new, non-creative activities to simply occupy your time and gently rediscover a sense of self through the present moment.",
      "source": "target",
